 ## Overview
-Simple Reflections is a local illumination technique that approximates specular highlights by raymarching along the geometric reflection vector at a surface hit point and blending the resulting color with the base surface color [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of rendering mirror-like surfaces in raymarched scenes without requiring complex recursive ray tracing or environment maps [S1, unofficial]. Unlike [Specular Reflections via Polynomial Expansion](1172-specular-reflections-via-polynomial-expansion.md), which uses polynomial expansion of the Phong term for analytical evaluation, Simple Reflections relies on iterative numerical raymarching [S1, S2, unofficial].
+Simple Reflections is a local illumination technique that approximates specular highlights by raymarching along the geometric reflection vector at a surface hit point and blending the resulting color with the base surface color [S1, S2, unofficial]. It calculates a simple reflection by raymarching off the surface normal and blending the result with the surface color [S1, unofficial]. Unlike [Specular Reflections via Polynomial Expansion](1172-specular-reflections-via-polynomial-expansion.md), which uses polynomial expansion of the Phong term for analytical evaluation, Simple Reflections relies on iterative numerical raymarching [S1, S2, unofficial].
 
